From: GibaxLeGrand <48137851+GibaxLeGrand@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 23:44:16 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Launcher: Online/LAN play, a room with HOST and CONNECT (up
 to 8 players)

On the PLAY page, ONLINE / LAN beside PLAY: HOST or CONNECT, the player's tag, the host's address or
the TCP port, the start state (a savestate made on Player Entry, the same file for everyone), "delay
based" (rollback greyed out, later). The room fills the launcher: P1 to P8 with their state (host,
ready, other start state, racing), the host's addresses to share, and the race the host sets (course,
laps, racers from the players to 8 with the AI driving the others, input delay); READY, START THE
RACE, LEAVE.

The relay runs in the host's launcher (launcher_online.cpp): the room's lines (JOIN, LREADY, LRULES,
LSTART, LGONE; WELCOME, MEMBERS, MATCH, ROOM), then the lockstep of tools/srnp/relais.py ported as
it is, on the same TCP port; the race's rules are the room's (a game's own RULES are left aside).
At START every launcher starts its game in the lobby through the game's menus (SRNP_LOBBY=2) with
its seat, from a user folder of its own (<user>/Online: the player's settings, their pad on port 4
for the relay, port 1 a keyless keyboard, their file mods turned on and copied there, the labels mod
srnp_etiquettes turned on when installed: without it the relay's Start did not get past Player
Entry). When every game has closed, the room is back.

Tests without clicks: SRNP_ONLINE_AUTO, _READY, _START, _RULES, _STATE, _ADDRESS, _TAG, _BACKGROUND;
SRNP_RUNNER for a launcher built apart from its runner.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
